// Lesson 9.2 — Hex, RGB & Data Abstraction
// expand-app CSP concept: hexadecimal, Color32 as 4 bytes, RGBA in the Inspector.
//
// GROUND TRUTH — read out of AP_CS_P_Starter_Project, not out of the old text:
//   * Every SpriteRenderer in every prefab (Coin, Player, Spikes, Turret,
//     Turret_Projectile, MobileEnemy, AxeItem, Switch) is still on its default
//     tint, m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}. Nothing in the game is tinted
//     from code — the colour you see is the artwork, not a value anybody typed.
//   * Coin.prefab draws guid 411fce3e…, which is Coin_Animation.png. Its
//     busiest pixel is #FFE681 = (255, 230, 129): that IS the coin's colour.
//   * Turret_Projectile.prefab draws Turret_Bullet.png, busiest pixel #008DF0.
//   * The stone ground tileset sliced into WallsTileSet/ is a desaturated grey:
//     busiest pixel #878579.
